# Documentation and working notes stay local. They go stale faster than the code they
# describe, and a wrong doc in a repo is read as true long after it stopped being true.
docs/
*/docs/
!**/README.md

# The long-form trust model. Same reasoning as docs/ above: it describes decisions rather than
# code, so it drifts, and the committed summary in README.md is the one outsiders should read.
ARCHITECTURE.md

# Research and claim-verification notes. Same reasoning: a snapshot of what the code said on
# one day, which stops being true the moment the code moves.
riset.md

# Assistant and editor scratch
.claude/
.cursor/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md

.DS_Store

# graphify knowledge graph output
graphify-out/
.graphifyignore
